  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:69130",
  "description": "OpenSSH is an SSH protocol implementation supported by a number of Linux, UNIX, and similar operating systems. It includes the core files necessary for both the OpenSSH client and server.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * openssh: OpenSSH: sftp client allows attacker to control downloaded file location (CVE-2026-59995)\n  * openssh: OpenSSH sshd: Security bypass due to incorrect handling of forwarding and tunneling options (CVE-2026-59999)\n  * openssh: OpenSSH: Tunnel forwarding restriction bypass (CVE-2026-73283)\n  * openssh: OpenSSH: ssh-agent allows remote execution of local operations (CVE-2026-73281)\n  * openssh: OpenSSH: Information disclosure and data corruption via use-after-free in ssh client (CVE-2026-73282)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
